# Cbm-Read-Check - optional configuration. Copy to `.env` beside the installed
# hook to override; the value below is the default.

# Where Codebase Memory MCP keeps its per-project databases. Blank means, in
# order: the CBM_CACHE_DIR environment variable; then the CBM_CACHE_DIR recorded
# in the matching CMM server's "env" block in the Claude JSON or Codex TOML
# client config; then the binary's own
# default (%USERPROFILE%\.cache\codebase-memory-mcp).
#
# The third step is the one that usually decides it. CBM_CACHE_DIR is normally
# set ONLY inside that server record, so the server process has it and a hook
# process never does - without that step the hook watches the default directory
# while the server writes somewhere else, and reports "no index yet" for ever.
# The hook is completely silent when <cache>\_config.db does not exist.
CBM_CACHE_DIR=

# Optional manual-CLI environment overrides. Blank values use the matching
# server record. CBM_RUNTIME_DIR also honors an explicit process override.
# The server's TEMP/TMP take precedence over the shell's generic temp defaults.
CBM_RUNTIME_DIR=
TEMP=
TMP=
